# Build artifacts. The container sets CARGO_TARGET_DIR outside this tree, but the
# macOS host uses the default — and this tree is a shared bind mount, so Linux and
# macOS artifacts must never collide here.
/target

# Cargo.lock IS committed: md2pdf is an application, not a library, and pinning
# the whole graph is the point. Do not add it here.

# Spike scratch
spikes/**/target
spikes/**/*.pdf
spikes/**/*.png
spikes/**/decisions.json

# Evidence rasters. The ladder is tuned by rendering a page and looking at it, so this
# tree accumulates PNGs faster than anything else in the repo — 27 of them from T26a2,
# T26b and T26c alone. They are *proof for a question already answered*: the finding
# they support is written up in design/, and the answer is what future readers need.
#
# So they are deliberately untracked (operator's call, 2026-08-23). Design docs cite
# them by path; a citation is a record of what was looked at, not a promise that the
# file is still in the tree. Regenerate by re-running the task's comparison.
design/evidence/

# Workbench session transcripts — tooling output, not project history.
.workbench/transcripts/
